# Line-ending normalization (CU-150, Rule 30).
#
# Text files are stored with LF in the repository. `text=auto` lets Git detect
# text vs. binary; `eol=lf` pins the working-tree ending to LF so a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true cannot rewrite tracked text to CRLF and make
# byte-level comparisons (golden baselines, checksummed reference data, MODTRAN
# decks) diverge across platforms. Where a written artifact's exact bytes matter,
# the writer also passes newline="\n" explicitly (belt-and-suspenders).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize or diff as text.
*.png   -text
*.jpg   -text
*.jpeg  -text
*.gif   -text
*.ico   -text
*.pdf   -text
*.xls   -text
*.xlsx  -text
*.npy   -text
*.npz   -text
*.h5    -text
*.hdf5  -text
*.zip   -text
*.gz    -text
*.ttf   -text
*.otf   -text
*.woff  -text
*.woff2 -text
